{
  "description": "A version 6 file's trackers (K123) normalise: a tracker needs an id of 1 to 64 letters, digits, - or _ (not __proto__), a kind the registry has, the first three ids their own kind (a diet tracker of kind strength drops), and a name that isn't blank, trimmed and cut to 60 characters. The first of each id wins. A bad position reads as the tracker's place in the list, a position is clamped to 0 to 10000, a daily target to 1 to 8 (its kind's default when it isn't a number, null for cardio whatever the file says), and a week that isn't a week key reads as null.",
